    "observations": [
      "The /caf grid renders u_caf_compliance_status faithfully, so it displays \"Compliant\" beside red control dots. The grid is not at fault; the field it reads is wrong.",
      "Suspected cause: business rule \"CAF - update BA when req compliant\" (after update, order 1500, filter caf_statusCHANGESTOin_compliance) sets the application compliant whenever ANY request goes compliant, without checking whether its siblings still are not.",
      "This falsifies HANDOFF section 3: \"An app is compliant only when every control is, matching the ServiceNow widget.\" The Salesforce LWC is documented as mirroring that behaviour, so the same wrong answer is likely on both platforms — see TC-INT-050."
    ],
    "expected": [
      "cmdb_ci_business_app.u_caf_compliance_status reads \"compliant\" only when EVERY CAF Request for that application is in_compliance.",
      "An application with any out_of_compliance control must not read compliant."
    ],
